    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "74578d52_3c7ded56",
        "filename": "board/coral/battery.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 102,
      "author": {
        "id": 1123814
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-09-08T16:36:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Due to your concerns I have changed these to look only at D-FET status. However, I still think this is a \"don\u0027t care\" if both FETs are checked. The FET status only has to be correct at least once so the battery can be reported as present. In my past testing even when the battery charge level is full, both the discharge and charge FETs will change their status to \u0027on\u0027 when coming out of battery cutoff mode. At some later point, the charge FET may indeed turn off, but initially, it will have been on when resuming from cutoff mode and that\u0027s really all these bits are being used to check. \n\nWhen I was looking at a similar issue on Eve, I was going to use just the D-FET status, but with this bit only, our HW team was still able to reproduce a case where power rail to H1 glitched when resuming from battery cutoff, but was not able to repro that when the status of both FETs was checked.",
      "parentUuid": "a28b25a2_18be3241",
      "revId": "03413df47d28801f016c64262a3a3caa2e7218fe",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "22178112_158cabbb",
        "filename": "board/coral/battery.c",
